back vice president kamala harris visits  the southern border for the first time  since being tapped to lead the biden  administration's response to the migrant  crisis  but some critics say she didn't do  enough white house correspondent peter  ducey is also on the ground in el paso  with some highlights from harris's visit  good evening peter  shannon good evening a few weeks ago  when the vice president went down to  central america  she warned migrants do not come  but today when she made her first trip  as vice president  to this side of the border she didn't  say that  i hope this does not sound trite or  corny  that we have the capacity to give people  hope closest the vice president got to  the border was  the inside of a dmv like port of entry  where people can walk across  and apply for asylum we have a line that  never stops the vice president didn't  spend much time at all talking about  illegal border crossers instead focusing  on the humanitarian  impact of recent surges this is this  issue cannot be reduced to a political  issue but that's what she did  at times it is here in el paso that the  previous administration's child  separation policy  was unveiled blaming the trump  administration for increased migration  we inherited a tough situation questions  about why the vp visited el paso  hundreds of miles away from the busiest  border crossings  have been answered i recommend it to the  vice president  that we visit el paso because it is one  of the busiest sectors on the border  busy is good according to the local  democratic congresswoman  welcome to el paso welcome to my  community to the new ellis island  the counterpoint comes from senator ted  cruz quote communities like el paso are  struggling because of the damage the  biden harris administration  has caused by opening the floodgates to  human smugglers and  drug cartels honestly this is a slap in  the face to the men and women that are  out there putting their lives on the  line  each and every day for at least 10 hours  a day  in areas which are a lot busier than  where she's going  she's getting the dog and pony show even  though the vice president has long  publicly claimed her focus is not on the  border  she says her trip to a border town was a  long time coming  how did you decide that right now was  the right time to make your first trip  to the border  well it's not my first trip i've been to  the border many times i'm the person in  charge of the response  so the important aspect of this visit  is leading this visit after  the work that we did in guatemala and  mexico because as i've long said i said  back in march i was going to come to the  border so this is not a new plan  the vice president did not mention  anything about those videos we've been  seeing lately of smugglers  freely ferrying people and drugs into  the country and she did not detail  what she thinks should happen to beef up  security at the most poorest parts of  the border instead  her focus was on trying to figure out  why it is that people leave home in the  first place instead of trying to figure  out  how to keep them home for now shannon  peter ducey traveling with vice  president thank you very much  and
 

